[0.052, "o", "[\r\n    {\r\n        \"chunkId\": 961,\r\n        \"documentId\": 905,\r\n        \"kind\": \"README\",\r\n        \"pathOrRef\": \"README.md\",\r\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/encode/httpx/blob/master/README.md\",\r\n        \"title\": \"README.md\",\r\n        \"headingPath\": \"Installation\",\r\n        \"snippet\": \"Install with pip: ```shell $ pip install httpx ``` Or, to include the optional HTTP/2 support, use: ```shell $ pip install httpx[http2] ``` HTTPX requires Python 3.9+.\",\r\n        \"score\": 0.031746031746031744,\r\n        \"vectorRank\": 3,\r\n        \"keywordRank\": 3\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"chunkId\": 1186,\r\n        \"documentId\": 919,\r\n        \"kind\": \"DOC\",\r\n        \"pathOrRef\": \"CHANGELOG.md\",\r\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/encode/httpx/blob/master/CHANGELOG.md\",\r\n        \"title\": \"CHANGELOG.md\",\r\n        \"headingPath\": \"Changelog > 0.13.0.dev2 (May 12th, 2020)\",\r\n        \"snippet\": \"The 0.13.0.dev2 is a *pre-release* version. To install it, use `pip install httpx --pre`.\",\r\n        \"score\": 0.029138513513513514,\r\n        \"vectorRank\": 4,\r\n        \"keywordRank\": 14\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"chunkId\": 1387,\r\n        \"documentId\": 955,\r\n        \"kind\": \"ISSUE\",\r\n        \"pathOrRef\": \"issue-947\",\r\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/encode/httpx/issues/947\",\r\n        \"title\": \"Version 1.0\",\r\n        \"headingPath\": \"Dependencies\",\r\n        \"snippet\": \"* `httpcore` * `h11` * `sniffio` * `rfc3986 ` * `idna` * `certifi` Optionals: `pip install httpx[http2]`, `pip install httpx[brotli]`\",\r\n        \"score\": 0.029116045245077504,\r\n        \"vectorRank\": 2,\r\n        \"keywordRank\": 17\r\n    }\r\n]\r\n"]
[1.009, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m== 4. Grounded answer with citations ==\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.683, "o", "{\r\n    \u001b[1m\"answer\"\u001b[0m: \u001b[32m\"To make a basic GET request with HTTPX you can use the top\\u2011level `httpx.get()` function for a synchronous call, e.g. `r = httpx.get(\\\"https://httpbin.org/status/500\\\")` [2]. For asynchronous code you can create an `AsyncClient` and call its `get()` method, e.g. `async with httpx.AsyncClient(http2=True) as client: r = await client.get(\\\"http://localhost:8080/hello\\\")` [4].\"\u001b[0m,\r\n    \u001b[1m\"citations\"\u001b[0m: [\r\n        {\r\n            \u001b[1m\"index\"\u001b[0m: \u001b[33m2\u001b[0m,\r\n            \u001b[1m\"title\"\u001b[0m: \u001b[32m\"Should error responses raise an HTTPError by default?\"\u001b[0m,\r\n            \u001b[1m\"url\"\u001b[0m: \u001b[32m\"https://github.com/encode/httpx/issues/752\"\u001b[0m,\r\n            \u001b[1m\"headingPath\"\u001b[0m: \u001b[32m\"Current situation and pain points\"\u001b[0m,\r\n            \u001b[1m\"snippet\"\u001b[0m: \u001b[32m\"Currently, to be notified of an error response we need to either: - Check the `.status_code` manually: ```python if response.status_code == 404: print(\\\"Not found\\\") if response.is_error: print(\\\"Error\\\") ``` - Call `.raise_for_status()`: ```python response.raise_for_status() # Raises an HTTPError ``` T...\"\u001b[0m\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n            \u001b[1m\"index\"\u001b[0m: \u001b[33m4\u001b[0m,\r\n            \u001b[1m\"title\"\u001b[0m: \u001b[32m\"How to force enable HTTP/2.0\"\u001b[0m,\r\n            \u001b[1m\"url\"\u001b[0m: \u001b[32m\"https://github.com/encode/httpx/issues/3261\"\u001b[0m,\r\n            \u001b[1m\"headingPath\"\u001b[0m: \u001b[32m\"\"\u001b[0m,\r\n            \u001b[1m\"snippet\"\u001b[0m: \u001b[32m\"I have an `HTTP/2.0` server and I want to ping/test it using an httpx client. I use this docs: https://www.python-httpx.org/http2/ And the client send this request ``` GET /hello HTTP/1.1\\\\r\\\\nHost: localhost:8080\\\\r\\\\nAccept: */*\\\\r\\\\nAccept-Encoding: gzip, deflate\\\\r\\\\nConnection: keep-alive\\\\r\\\\nUser-Agent...\"\u001b[0m\r\n        }\r\n    ],\r\n    \u001b[1m\"refused\"\u001b[0m: \u001b[1;34mfalse\u001b[0m,\r\n    \u001b[1m\"latencyMs\"\u001b[0m: \u001b[33m632\u001b[0m,\r\n    \u001b[1m\"cached\"\u001b[0m: \u001b[1;34mfalse\u001b[0m\r\n}\r\n"]
